# AWS Secrets Manager and IAM Role Provisioning with Terraform

This Terraform configuration automates the secure setup of an AWS Secrets Manager secret and provisions an IAM role for Amazon EC2 instances along with an inline policy for secret retrieval.

## Resources Provisioned

1. **AWS Secrets Manager Secret** (`aws_secretsmanager_secret` & `aws_secretsmanager_secret_version`):
   - Stores application credentials securely (`datacenter-app-secret`).
2. **IAM Role** (`aws_iam_role`):
   - Creates an IAM role (`datacenter-app-role`) allowing EC2 instances as the trusted entity (via `sts:AssumeRole`).
3. **Inline IAM Policy** (`aws_iam_role_policy`):
   - Attaches an inline policy (`datacenter-app-policy`) granting `secretsmanager:GetSecretValue` and `secretsmanager:DescribeSecret` permissions scoped to the created secret.

## Variables (`variables.tf`)

| Variable Name | Description | Default Value |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| `KKE_SECRET_NAME` | Name of the secret in AWS Secrets Manager | `datacenter-app-secret` |
| `KKE_SECRET_VALUE` | Secret payload string | `{"db_user":"admin","db_pass":"supersecret"}` |
| `KKE_ROLE_NAME` | Name of the IAM Role for EC2 | `datacenter-app-role` |
| `KKE_POLICY_NAME` | Name of the inline IAM Policy | `datacenter-app-policy` |

## Outputs (`outputs.tf`)

- `KKE_secret_name`: Displays the provisioned secret name.
- `KKE_role_name`: Displays the provisioned IAM role name.
- `KKE_policy_name`: Displays the provisioned inline policy name.

## Usage / Verification

Initialize and apply the configuration from the Terraform working directory (`/home/bob/terraform`):

```bash
terraform init
terraform apply -auto-approve
To verify that your infrastructure is fully synchronized and matches the desired state:

Bash
terraform plan
